# Suggested Hooks — fastapi

## Stack Summary

| Tool | Version / Source | Config Location |
|------|-----------------|-----------------|
| Ruff (lint + format) | `>=0.14.14` (dev dep) | `[tool.ruff.*]` in `pyproject.toml` |
| mypy | `>=1.14.1` (dev dep), strict mode | `[tool.mypy]` in `pyproject.toml` |
| ty | `>=0.0.9` (dev dep) | n/a (no config section) |
| pytest | `>=9.0.0` with xdist, timeout=20s | `[tool.pytest]` in `pyproject.toml` |
| pre-commit | ruff, mypy, ty hooks via `uv run` | `.pre-commit-config.yaml` |

---

## Hook 1 — Ruff Lint Auto-Fix

Automatically fixes lint issues when Python files are written or edited.

FastAPI's ruff config selects rules E, W, F, I (isort), B (bugbear), C4 (comprehensions), and UP (pyupgrade), with intentional ignores for E501 (line length), B008 (function calls in defaults — core FastAPI pattern), C901 (complexity), and W191 (tabs). Extensive per-file ignores exist for `docs_src/` tutorial files. Running ruff automatically prevents import ordering, unused imports, and style issues from accumulating between commits.

Add to `.claude/settings.json`:
```json
{
  "hooks": {
    "postToolExecution": [
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit",
        "command": "ruff check --fix \"$FILE_PATH\"",
        "description": "Auto-fix lint issues with ruff (E/W/F/I/B/C4/UP rules)"
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

**Setup**: `pip install ruff` or `uv sync` (already in `docs-tests` dependency group: `ruff >=0.14.14`)

---

## Hook 2 — Ruff Format Check

Checks formatting on written Python files and reports deviations without auto-fixing, so you see the diff before committing.

FastAPI runs `ruff format` across `fastapi/`, `tests/`, `docs_src/`, and `scripts/`. The pre-commit hook uses `--exit-non-zero-on-format` to block malformatted commits. A post-write check catches formatting drift immediately rather than at commit time.

Add to `.claude/settings.json`:
```json
{
  "hooks": {
    "postToolExecution": [
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit",
        "command": "ruff format --check --diff \"$FILE_PATH\"",
        "description": "Check ruff formatting on changed Python files"
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

**Setup**: Same `ruff` install as above. To auto-format instead of just checking, replace `--check --diff` with just the file path: `ruff format "$FILE_PATH"`.

---

## Hook 3 — mypy Type Checking (Framework Source)

Runs mypy in strict mode on the `fastapi/` package when framework source files are modified.

mypy is configured with `strict = true` and the `pydantic.mypy` plugin in `pyproject.toml`. The pre-commit config runs `mypy fastapi` (not per-file) because mypy needs full-project context for accurate type resolution. This hook scopes to the `fastapi/` directory to avoid running on `docs_src/` (which has relaxed type checking overrides) or `tests/`.

Add to `.claude/settings.json`:
```json
{
  "hooks": {
    "postToolExecution": [
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit",
        "command": "if echo \"$FILE_PATH\" | grep -q '^fastapi/'; then mypy fastapi --no-error-summary 2>&1 | head -30; fi",
        "description": "Run mypy strict check on fastapi/ source changes"
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

**Setup**: `pip install mypy` (already in `tests` dependency group: `mypy >=1.14.1`). Requires `pydantic` installed for the mypy plugin.

**Note**: mypy runs on the whole `fastapi/` package (not per-file) because strict mode with the Pydantic plugin needs full project context. Output is truncated to 30 lines to keep feedback fast.

---

## Hook 4 — Pytest for Modified Test Files

Runs the specific test file when a test file is modified, with the required `PYTHONPATH` set.

FastAPI's test suite requires `PYTHONPATH=./docs_src` because tests import tutorial examples from `docs_src/` as modules. Tests have a 20-second timeout and run with `pytest-xdist`. This hook runs only the changed test file (not the full suite) to keep feedback under a few seconds.

Add to `.claude/settings.json`:
```json
{
  "hooks": {
    "postToolExecution": [
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit",
        "command": "if echo \"$FILE_PATH\" | grep -qE '^tests/.*\\.py$'; then PYTHONPATH=./docs_src pytest \"$FILE_PATH\" -x --timeout=20 --no-header -q 2>&1 | tail -20; fi",
        "description": "Run modified test file with PYTHONPATH=./docs_src"
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

**Setup**: `pip install pytest pytest-timeout` (already in `tests` dependency group). Also install test dependencies: `uv sync` or `pip install -e ".[all]"` plus the test extras.

---

## Hook 5 — Large File Warning

Warns when a file exceeds 500 lines, which helps catch overgrown modules.

FastAPI's core source files are deliberately compact — most are under 300 lines. The largest (`routing.py`, `dependencies/utils.py`) are around 800–1000 lines and are already considered complex. A 500-line threshold flags when a file is growing beyond the norm for this codebase, prompting a refactoring conversation before it becomes unwieldy.

Add to `.claude/settings.json`:
```json
{
  "hooks": {
    "postToolExecution": [
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit",
        "command": "LINE_COUNT=$(wc -l < \"$FILE_PATH\"); if [ \"$LINE_COUNT\" -gt 500 ]; then echo \"⚠️  Warning: $FILE_PATH is $LINE_COUNT lines (threshold: 500)\"; fi",
        "description": "Warn if file exceeds 500 lines"
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

**Setup**: No additional tools needed — uses standard shell commands.

---

## Combined Configuration

Here is the complete `.claude/settings.json` with all hooks merged:

```json
{
  "hooks": {
    "postToolExecution": [
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit",
        "command": "ruff check --fix \"$FILE_PATH\"",
        "description": "Auto-fix lint issues with ruff"
      },
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit",
        "command": "ruff format --check --diff \"$FILE_PATH\"",
        "description": "Check ruff formatting on changed files"
      },
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit",
        "command": "if echo \"$FILE_PATH\" | grep -q '^fastapi/'; then mypy fastapi --no-error-summary 2>&1 | head -30; fi",
        "description": "Run mypy strict check on fastapi/ source changes"
      },
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit",
        "command": "if echo \"$FILE_PATH\" | grep -qE '^tests/.*\\.py$'; then PYTHONPATH=./docs_src pytest \"$FILE_PATH\" -x --timeout=20 --no-header -q 2>&1 | tail -20; fi",
        "description": "Run modified test file with PYTHONPATH=./docs_src"
      },
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit",
        "command": "LINE_COUNT=$(wc -l < \"$FILE_PATH\"); if [ \"$LINE_COUNT\" -gt 500 ]; then echo \"⚠️  Warning: $FILE_PATH is $LINE_COUNT lines (threshold: 500)\"; fi",
        "description": "Warn if file exceeds 500 lines"
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

---

## Hooks NOT Suggested (and Why)

| Tool | Why Excluded |
|------|-------------|
| **ty** (type checker) | The repo uses `ty check fastapi` in pre-commit and lint scripts, but `ty` is a very new tool (v0.0.9) with rapidly changing behavior. Running it as a post-write hook would likely produce noisy, unstable output. Better left for pre-commit or manual runs until it stabilizes. |
| **Black** | Not used for formatting — the repo uses `ruff format`. Black is only a docs dependency for code rendering in MkDocs. |
| **ESLint / TypeScript** | Not applicable — this is a pure Python project. |
| **Coverage** | `pytest-cov` is installed but coverage is a full-suite metric, not useful as a per-file post-write hook. |
| **pre-commit run** | The `.pre-commit-config.yaml` includes doc-related hooks (permalinks, README generation, translation fixes) that are expensive and irrelevant during development. The individual tool hooks above are faster and more targeted. |

