## Hook 1 — Ruff Lint Auto-Fix

Automatically fixes lint issues when Python files are written or edited.

This repo enforces ruff linting with rules `E, W, F, I, B, C4, UP` and intentionally ignores `E501` (line length) and `B008` (function calls in defaults — required for `Query()`, `Depends()`, etc.). The `--force-exclude` flag ensures per-file ignores from `pyproject.toml` are respected, which is critical here since FastAPI has 30+ per-file rule overrides for tutorial code in `docs_src/`.

Add to `.claude/settings.json`:
```json
{
  "hooks": {
    "postToolExecution": [
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit",
        "command": "ruff check --fix --force-exclude \"$FILE_PATH\"",
        "description": "Auto-fix lint issues with ruff"
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

**Setup**: `uv sync --group tests` (ruff is already in the `docs-tests` dependency group, included by `tests`)

