## Hook 3 — mypy Strict Type Checking

Runs mypy on the `fastapi/` package when framework source files are modified.

mypy is configured in **strict mode** with the `pydantic.mypy` plugin, meaning every function must have full type annotations. The config includes overrides that relax rules for `docs_src/` (no `disallow_untyped_defs`) and `fastapi.concurrency` (ignore missing imports). This hook targets only `fastapi/` source changes — running mypy on the full codebase for every edit would be too slow, and `docs_src/` files have relaxed rules anyway.

Add to `.claude/settings.json`:
```json
{
  "hooks": {
    "postToolExecution": [
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit",
        "command": "case \"$FILE_PATH\" in */fastapi/*.py) mypy fastapi ;; esac",
        "description": "Type-check fastapi/ with mypy (strict mode + pydantic plugin)"
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

**Setup**: `uv sync --group tests` (mypy `>=1.14.1` is in the tests dependency group)

