## Hook 6 — Large File Warning

Warns when a file exceeds 750KB, matching the pre-commit `check-added-large-files` threshold.

The `.pre-commit-config.yaml` already enforces `--maxkb=750` (with `uv.lock` excluded). This hook catches oversized files before they reach the commit stage, which is especially relevant given the large `docs_src/` directory with hundreds of tutorial files.

Add to `.claude/settings.json`:
```json
{
  "hooks": {
    "postToolExecution": [
      {
        "matcher": "Write",
        "command": "if [ -f \"$FILE_PATH\" ]; then size=$(wc -c < \"$FILE_PATH\"); if [ \"$size\" -gt 768000 ]; then echo \"WARNING: $FILE_PATH is $(($size / 1024))KB — exceeds 750KB limit from .pre-commit-config.yaml\"; fi; fi",
        "description": "Warn if file exceeds 750KB (pre-commit threshold)"
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

**Setup**: No additional installation needed — uses standard shell commands.

